    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1527">

                <pb facs="0982" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/305.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of November 19, enclosing [etc.]</p>
                <p>It is noted that you suggest that the Admiral in command in Mexican east coast
                    waters be instructed to extend such protection as may be possible to the lives
                    and properties of Americans, British, and. other foreigners at Tampico, as well
                    as to afford them refuge in the event of danger.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that the Commander in Chief of the Detached
                    Squadron in Mexican waters has been directed accordingly.</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
